# requirements-speech.in : the speech check's environment (qa_speech.py, Q806 and Q807: faster-whisper base.en on the
# CPU), a side Python 3.14 environment, so engine/requirements.txt stays Pillow and numpy only. These lines are the
# one place the pins live; qa_speech.py runs the compiled lock. After a change, compile the lock again from this folder:
#   uv pip compile --universal --generate-hashes --python-version 3.14 requirements-speech.in -o requirements-speech.txt
# qa_speech.py hashes requirements-speech.txt into every transcript's cache key, so a new lock transcribes again.
# envs.py builds the environment from the lock with uv pip install --require-hashes, so a wheel whose sha256 differs
# from the lock's is refused. NOT installed by setup.sh. The model is a separate download
# (python qa_speech.py fetch), never fetched without the user's yes.
# Every package that changes the words is pinned here. Clips go in as raw float32, so faster-whisper never opens a file
# itself; av stays below 19 anyway (its file path fails with av 19, SYSTRAN/faster-whisper#1589, fixed on main, not in
# the 1.2.1 release). Versions read from PyPI on 2026-10-28, 2026-11-03 and 2026-11-16 (ctranslate2 4.9.0, onnxruntime
# 1.32.0, numpy 2.5.5).
faster-whisper==1.2.1
ctranslate2==4.9.0
av==18.1.0
onnxruntime==1.32.0
tokenizers==0.23.3
numpy==2.5.5
